Title: Cover EXIT trap gaps in test_new test_update test_ready
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude
Closed: done

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created

2026-05-05T11:52Z claude closed — done
--- body ---
Three test scripts allocate `mktemp -d` directories that are not covered by
their `EXIT` trap. If `set -eu` causes early exit after allocation but before
the inline cleanup, the directory leaks.

**`tests/test_new.sh`** — `WDIR=$(mktemp -d)` at line ~139 is cleaned up
inline at lines ~147-148 but is not in the `trap` at line 13. If any assertion
between allocation and cleanup fails, `WDIR` leaks.

**`tests/test_update.sh`** — `TICKET_DIR` and `WORKSPACE` (both `mktemp -d`)
are cleaned up inline but neither is covered by the `trap` at line 34 (which
only covers `SRV_DIR`). Early-exit leaks both.

**`tests/test_ready.sh`** — `tmpdir` at line ~403 is cleaned up at line ~418
but is outside the trap at line 14.

**Fix:** For each affected file, add the secondary temp directory to the trap
at the top of the file (or declare a cleanup function that removes all of them).
The safest pattern: declare all temp dirs at the top with empty values and
include all in one `trap 'rm -rf "$A" "$B" "$C"' EXIT`.
